      "writtenOn": "2025-03-05T16:48:34Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Do we need any mutex locking in these APIs?  How do we handle when thread1 logs \"hello world\" and thread2 logs \"foobar\" at the same time?",
      "revId": "870d0469e3825b91230c2ccb0fcf2b28bf66f3cb",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "97757a08_9618139e",
        "filename": "common/panic_log.c",
        "patchSetId": 13
      },
      "lineNbr": 116,
      "author": {
        "id": 1390635
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-03-06T18:19:14Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Maybe. Conflicting writes will result in the checksum failing and the panic log being discarded. Locking doubles the execution time of preserved_ring_buf_write. I think the trade off favors not locking in favor of improved performance and accepting that the panic log may be corrupted in rare cases. I could add locking as an option if desired.",
      "parentUuid": "7a1d9839_e270ca6f",
      "revId": "870d0469e3825b91230c2ccb0fcf2b28bf66f3cb",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
